{"id":"memorial_102605","cat":"memorial","group":{"id":"memorial102600","label":"Call Logs · Jonathan_report"},"label":"daywhatever.mp4","stage":null,"prev":"memorial_102604","next":null,"speakers":{},"icons":{},"lines":[{"id":"memorial_102605_1","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"(File corrupted, audio only)"},{"id":"memorial_102605_2","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"The last Nikke has expired. No, that's not right. She had a name. Della. Della has died."},{"id":"memorial_102605_3","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"She finally succumbed to Mind Switch. She thought she had been redeemed and would ascend to heaven."},{"id":"memorial_102605_4","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"I remained by her side for some time after she went."},{"id":"memorial_102605_5","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"Without any Nikkes to protect me, there is no chance of me surviving on the surface. Spending a few moments to mourn her wouldn't do me any harm."},{"id":"memorial_102605_6","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"(Silence)"},{"id":"memorial_102605_7","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"(Silence)"},{"id":"memorial_102605_8","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"(Silence)"},{"id":"memorial_102605_9","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"I'm losing strength."},{"id":"memorial_102605_10","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"The cold has become oddly comforting."},{"id":"memorial_102605_11","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"I can see something through the broken window of my hideout."},{"id":"memorial_102605_12","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"I can see heaven so clearly now. It seems so real, like it never disappeared."},{"id":"memorial_102605_13","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"I wish I could go there."},{"id":"memorial_102605_14","type":"Speech","speaker":null,"key":"Locale_Memorial:memorial_26_05_description","text":"At this point, experiencing a Mind Switch would be a relief for me."}]}